    "collapsible_tabs_BiwnEG": {
      "type": "collapsible-tabs",
      "blocks": {
        "question_EFwCbL": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is CBD?",
            "answer": "<p>CBD (short for cannabidiol) is a naturally occurring, non-intoxicating cannabinoid found in the hemp plant. However, CBD isn’t the only hemp-derived compound worth noting. Several secondary cannabinoids and flavorful terpenes work in synergy alongside CBD in our full-spectrum hemp products.<br/><br/>To learn more, read this <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/pages/what-is-cbd\" title=\"Learn more about CBD\">guide to CBD</a>.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_ydcDcP": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What are the benefits of CBD?",
            "answer": "<p>CBD helps to balance the various systems of the body. It is said to promote relaxation, homeostasis, and an overall sense of calm by working with the endocannabinoid system, which you can learn more about on <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/blogs/blog/what-is-the-endocannabinoid-system\" title=\"Read about CBD and the endocannabinoid system in our blog\">our blog</a>. It may also help reduce inflammation.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_9raebi": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What are the benefits of CBN?",
            "answer": "<p>Cannabinol (CBN) is said to promote sleep, stimulate appetite, and foster bone growth. CBN provides anti-inflammatory and analgesic effects. Understanding <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/blogs/blog/everything-you-should-know-about-cbn\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">what is CBN in edibles </span></a>can help you determine whether a CBN-infused product is right for your sleep routine.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_VjBqYW": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What are cannabinoids?",
            "answer": "<p>Cannabinoids are compounds found in cannabis (both hemp and marijuana) plants.<br/><br/>Of these, CBD and THC are the most abundant and therefore the most studied cannabinoids. However, there are well over 100 trace compounds in cannabis with potential benefits we have yet to explore.<br/><br/>Incredibly, our bodies are naturally wired with receptors that interact with the cannabinoids found in cannabis.<br/><br/>Read about <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/pages/what-is-cbd\" title=\"What is CBD?\">the cannabinoids</a> found in HempLucid products.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_39PBP8": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What are terpenes?",
            "answer": "<p>Terpenes (pronounced tur-peens) and flavonoids give cannabis its unique smell and flavor. These aromatic compounds are also found in fruit, spices, and other plants to produce scents ranging from sweet citrus to more pungent odors. Beyond simply producing smells, terpenes also work in synergy with cannabinoids to contribute to the entourage effect within the body’s endocannabinoid system.<br/><br/>Read about <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/blogs/blog/benefits-of-terpenes\" title=\"Benefits of Terpenes\">the terpenes</a> found in HempLucid products.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_ntdmTG": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How does CBD work and what is the endocannabinoid system?",
            "answer": "<p>The benefits associated with CBD and other hemp-derived compounds can be experienced thanks to a widespread network of cannabinoid receptors known as the endocannabinoid system, or ECS. The role of the ECS is to maintain a physiological balance, homeostasis, in processes throughout the body.<br/><br/>The endocannabinoid system is located in the mammalian brain and throughout the central and peripheral nervous systems. It consists of neuromodulatory lipids and their receptors. There are two main types of receptors in the ECS: CB1 and CB2. CB1 receptors are primarily located in the central nervous system and brains of mammals, and CB2 receptors are generally found in the peripheral nervous system.<br/><br/>When you add CBD to your daily routine, alongside a healthy diet and exercise, you’re supporting the many functions of your endocannabinoid system.<br/><br/>To learn more, <a href=\"/blogs/blog/what-is-the-endocannabinoid-system\" title=\"What does the endocannabinoid system do?\">watch this video</a> about the endocannabinoid system.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_WGMij3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How much CBD should I take?",
            "answer": "<p>There’s no one-size-fits-all when it comes to CBD. Everyone is different and will respond to hemp extracts in different ways. Finding your ideal strength and serving might require some adjustment over time and may even differ day-to-day depending on how you partake, whether you’ve eaten, and your unique metabolism.<br/><br/>We encourage users to follow the serving size on the product packaging and adjust as needed. More detailed information on things like Best Results, Suggested Use, and Tips & Tricks can be found on each product page.<br/><br/>If you’re just starting out, you might start with a lower amount and increase as needed. If you’ve used cannabinoids before, you might know that a greater strength is best for you. The goal is always a feeling of balance, whatever that means for you.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_F7VMac": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How much CBD should I give to my pet?",
            "answer": "<p>Because our pets also have an endocannabinoid system, we developed a line of hemp-derived CBD just for them. Our four-legged companions come in all shapes and sizes, so while we can offer general guidelines, it’s best to start low. From there, adjust as needed to find the ideal serving for your pet.<br/><br/>We encourage users to follow the serving size on the product packaging and adjust as needed. More detailed information on things like Best Results, Suggested Use, and Tips & Tricks can be found on each product page.<br/><br/>Typical suggested servings start at 1mg to 5mg of CBD per 10lbs of body weight.<br/><br/>Shop HempLucid's line of <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/collections/pets-cbd\" title=\"Shop CBD for Pets\">CBD oil for pets</a>.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_4XLmxY": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What should I expect when taking CBD?",
            "answer": "<p>Everyone is unique and may have a slightly different experience when taking CBD. For most people, CBD as a daily supplement can provide a general sense of balance and well-being by supporting the endocannabinoid system. This is often described as a feeling of calm, relaxation, and relief from everyday stresses.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_KcTUCM": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Will CBD get me high?",
            "answer": "<p>No. HempLucid products are derived from a hemp genetic that contains less than 0.3% THC, the cannabinoid that causes the high associated with marijuana. Our CBD products are non-intoxicating.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_MPefWJ": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What’s the difference between CBD and THC?",
            "answer": "<p>CBD (cannabidiol) and THC (tetrahydrocannabinol) are the two most abundant cannabinoids found in cannabis plants. However, each of these compounds interacts with the body in different ways.<br/><br/>CBD is non-intoxicating and supports the function of the endocannabinoid system by working alongside other phytocannabinoids (from a plant) and endogenous cannabinoids (produced by the body).<br/><br/>THC has a strong binding affinity with receptors in the ECS and is responsible for the high associated with marijuana. However, in the trace amounts found in hemp, THC is more subtle. Rather than causing a euphoric high, traces of THC complement the entourage effect experienced when consuming full-spectrum hemp extracts.<br/><br/>Watch <a href=\"/pages/what-is-cbd\" title=\"What's the difference between hemp and marijuana?\">this video</a> about the difference between hemp products and marijuana.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_zgit4U": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is full-spectrum CBD?",
            "answer": "<p>In our products, the term “full-spectrum” refers to an extract that contains all the compounds found in our premium hemp genetics. This includes CBD, several secondary cannabinoids (including trace amounts of THC), and a robust terpene profile. HempLucid’s full-spectrum CBD is the only way to experience the complete synergy offered by the hemp plant, also known as the entourage effect.<br/><br/><a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/collections/full-spectrum-whole-plant-cbd\" title=\"Shop  full-spectrum CBD products\">Shop HempLucid's line of full-spectrum CBD products</a>.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_37N8bL": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is broad-spectrum CBD?",
            "answer": "<p>Broad-spectrum extracts offer the benefits of CBD, secondary cannabinoids, and flavorful terpenes with non-detectable levels of THC. Selecting the right extract type depends on your individual needs, and you can <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/blogs/blog/comparing-cbd-isolate-full-spectrum-and-broad-spectrum-cbd-which-is-right-for-you\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">learn about cbd isolate vs full spectrum</span></a> to compare all three options side by side.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_DntyqF": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is CBD isolate?",
            "answer": "<p>CBD isolate, as the name implies, is just that: isolated CBD. We understand the trace amounts of THC found in our whole-plant extracts aren’t compatible with everyone’s lifestyle. Our THC-free line of products offers the benefits of CBD without secondary cannabinoids or other hemp compounds. Fortunately, even isolated CBD can support the endocannabinoid system in balancing processes throughout the body.<br/><br/>In our CBD isolate products, we re-introduce terpenes to encourage the entourage effect while keeping the products THC-free.<br/><br/>Shop HempLucid's line of <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/collections/thc-free-cbd\" title=\"Shop THC-Free CBD\">CBD Isolate</a> products.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        }
      },
